  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0506\" is used to manage the construction of an electrical grid infrastructure project. It consists of 11 tables, each representing a different aspect of the project. The tables are interconnected through foreign keys, which ensure referential integrity and data consistency.\nThe \"construction_management_unit\" table contains information about the construction management units involved in the project, including their names, contact numbers, responsible persons, and associated projects. The \"business_project_department_progress\" table tracks the progress of business project departments, including their names, responsible persons, and project progress.\nThe \"resource_allocation\" table manages the allocation of resources to projects, including the resources' types, quantities, and allocation statuses. The \"collaborative_task\" table tracks the progress of collaborative tasks, including their names, responsible persons, task progress, and task priorities.\nThe \"supervision_project_department\" table manages the supervision of project departments, including their names, responsible persons, resource allocations, and personnel management. The \"electrical_grid_infrastructure_project\" table contains information about the electrical grid infrastructure project, including its name, construction progress, resource allocation, quality control, safety management, and project department.\nThe \"resource_table\" table manages the resources used in the project, including their types, quantities, and allocation statuses. The \"collaborative_work_platform\" table tracks the progress of collaborative work platforms, including their names, responsible persons, task progress, task priorities, and completion statuses.\nThe \"project_management\" table manages the management of projects, including their names, unit IDs, construction progress, resource allocation, quality control, and safety management. The \"project_department_management\" table tracks the management of project departments, including their names, project IDs, project progress, and issue reporting.\nThe \"supervision_department_management\" table manages the supervision of department management, including their names, project IDs, resource allocation, and personnel management.\nOverall, the schema is designed to ensure data consistency, referential integrity, and data management for the construction of an electrical grid infrastructure project.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\n1.Construction Management Unit Module:Login to the construction management system, select individual projects, create projects and route sections, determine annual project plans, and view data for the project team. This includes:Unit Name, Contact Number, Responsible Person, Associated Project, Annual Plan.Each unit contains multiple electrical grid infrastructure projects.\n2.Business Project Department Module:\nManage project progress, including planning, summarizing, report reviews, etc., and report encountered issues.Records include:Project Department ID, Department Name, Responsible Person, Project Progress, and Issue Reporting.Each project department contains multiple electrical grid infrastructure projects.\n3.Supervision Project Department Module:Display resources and management overview of the supervision department in a static web page format.Includes:Supervision Department Name, Responsible Person, Resource Allocation, Personnel Management.Each supervision department supervises multiple construction management units.\n4.Electrical Grid Infrastructure Projects:Each electrical grid infrastructure project includes:\nProject ID, Project Name, Construction Progress, Resource Allocation, Quality Control, Safety Management.\n5.Resources:Manage and allocate resources such as human and material resources effectively to improve utilization and reduce costs.Records include:Resource Type, Resource Quantity.Each project can be assigned multiple resources, and each resource can be used by multiple projects. Resource allocation and usage records need to be kept.\n6.Collaborative Work Platform:Supports task assignment, progress tracking, and feedback on completion status.Every task includes:Task Name, Responsible Person, Task Progress, Task Priority, Completion Status.Each task includes multiple electrical grid infrastructure projects.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0506.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0506\nCREATE TABLE `construction_management_unit` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `construction_management_unit_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `electrical_grid_infrastructure_project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `business_project_department_progress` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `progress` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `resource_allocation` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `resource_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `allocation_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `resource_allocation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `electrical_grid_infrastructure_project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `collaborative_task` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `progress` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `priority` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supervision_project_department` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `resource_allocation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `supervision_project_department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`resource_allocation_id`) REFERENCES `resource_allocation` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `electrical_grid_infrastructure_project` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `construction_progress` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `resource_allocation` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quality_control` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `safety_management` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `resource_table` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `resource_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `allocation_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `collaborative_work_platform` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `task_progress` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `task_priority` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `completion_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_management` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `construction_progress` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `resource_allocation` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `quality_control` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `safety_management` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_department_management` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `progress` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `issue_reporting` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_department_management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `electrical_grid_infrastructure_project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supervision_department_management` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `resource_allocation` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `supervision_department_management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `electrical_grid_infrastructure_project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
